          "title": "You'll want to know: इन्द्रियम्",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इन्द्रियम् — indriyam — \"a sense; an organ of sense\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "नरस्य पञ्च इन्द्रियाणि सन्ति। narasya pañca indriyāṇi santi. A person has five senses."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इन्द्रियम् (indriyam) is built on Indra, the god's name: MW's first sense is \"belonging to Indra\", then \"bodily power\" and \"a sense, an organ of sense\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
